"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.06706433034410775,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":13.2,"_gate_rev_durability":0.07887220969833342,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":64.4,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.024747721072239017,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":38.6,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.31687,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Nelnet, Inc. engages in loan servicing, education technology services, and payment businesses worldwide. The company operates through four segments: Loan Servicing and Systems, Education Technology Services and Payments, Asset Generation and Management, and Nelnet Bank. The Loan Servicing and Systems segment provides loan conversion, application processing, borrower updates, customer, payment processing, due diligence procedures, funds management reconciliation, and claim processing services. This segment also offers student loan servicing software; and business process outsourcing services primarily in contact center management, such as inbound calls, outreach campaigns and sales, and interacting with customers through multi-channels, and processing and administrative services. The Education Technology Services and Payments segment provides financial management services; school information system software; a donation platform; education technology solutions; and customized professional development and coaching, and advanced learning and educational instruction services. This segment also offers tuition payment plans, and service and technology for student billings, payments, and refunds; solutions for in-person, online, and mobile payment experiences on campus; payment processing services, such as credit card and electronic transfer; learning management system; an integrated commerce payment platform; and a school management platform that provides administrative, information and financial management, and communication functions for K-12 schools. The Asset Generation and Management segment invest, allocates an manages loan assts. The Nelnet Bank segment operates as an internet industrial bank. It also offers investment advisory, investment, and reinsurance services, as well as engages in the real estate investment; and solar engineering, procurement, and construction businesses. The company was founded in 1977 and is headquartered in Lincoln, Nebraska.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jeffrey R. Noordhoek | Chief Executive Officer | Age 59 | Compensation: $2.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 5K people. Each employee generates $69K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Nelnet, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $4.5B market cap.","The top line has compounded at +13% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 2% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $397M in free cash flow, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.99\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 11.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.5% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 32% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.3pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 55/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 27% margin of safety against estimated fair value","19 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Trading Systems Reacting to (NNI) Volatility","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/43/Trading_Systems_Reacting_to_NNI_Volatility_111226053802_1794523082.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794523082.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Nelnet (NNI) Looks Pricey As Third Quarter Earnings Weaken","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nyse-nni/nelnet/news/nelnet-nni-looks-pricey-as-third-quarter-earnings-weaken","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794479510.678,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.402,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Head to Head Comparison: Nelnet (NYSE:NNI) vs. Qfin (NASDAQ:QFIN)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/head-to-head-comparison-nelnet-nysenni-vs-qfin-nasdaqqfin.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794461324.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.893,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Nelnet (NYSE:NNI) Posts Earnings Results, Beats Estimates By $0.06 EPS","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/08/nelnet-nysenni-posts-earnings-results-beats-estimates-by-0-06-eps.html","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794119212.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.796,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Nelnet declares $0.36 dividend (NYSE:NNI)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4668135-nelnet-declares-0_36-dividend","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793973452.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Will Earnings Drop Change Nelnet (NNI) Stoc